{#
    Overrides Sylius' own
    @SyliusCore/Email/Blocks/OrderConfirmation/_content.html.twig
    (standard Symfony bundle-template-override mechanism -
    templates/bundles/<Bundle class name>/<path>, NOT a vendor-code edit).

    LOCATION MATTERS - DO NOT MOVE THIS INTO sulu-overlay/:
    order confirmation mails are sent by SYLIUS, so this override has to
    live in the Sylius app's own templates/ directory (the project root).
    It originally sat in sulu-overlay/templates/bundles/, which made
    make sulu-theme copy it into the Sulu app - where nothing ever reads
    it. It was silently ineffective for two versions until a customer-
    facing mail still showed the dead link this file is meant to remove
    (see FIXES.md No. 45).

    Why this exists: the original template's "view order / change payment
    method" button links to sylius_shop_order_show - a page belonging to
    Sylius' own shop frontend, which is switched off in this headless
    setup (see FIXES.md No. 23). The link would lead nowhere, and its
    label promises a "change payment method" capability that was never
    built in the Sulu frontend either. Removing the button was chosen
    over pointing it at our own /checkout/bestaetigung/{number} page,
    since that page is only meant for the moment right after checkout,
    not as a standing order-lookup page for a mail opened days later
    (see FIXES.md No. 34 for the full reasoning).

    Everything else is identical to the original: order number and
    "thank you" text stay exactly as Sylius renders them.
#}
<div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    {{ 'sylius.email.order_confirmation.your_order_number'|trans({}, null, localeCode) }}
    <div style="margin: 10px 0;">
      <span style="border: 1px solid #eee; padding: 10px; color: #1abb9c; font-size: 28px;">
        {{ order.number }}
      </span>
    </div>
    {{ 'sylius.email.order_confirmation.has_been_successfully_placed'|trans({}, null, localeCode) }}
</div>

<div style="text-align: center;">
    {{ 'sylius.email.order_confirmation.thank_you'|trans({}, null, localeCode) }}
</div>
